100-- [Internationalization (I18N)](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/i18n.md) — English | Русский
101-- [Layout components and spacings](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/layout.md) — This guide covers UIKit's layout foundations: a shared spacing scale (--g-spacing-*, used everywhere via tokens and props) and a responsive grid (Container/Row/Col), plus the flexbox-based Flex/Box primitives built on top of them. Compose pages from these instead of raw divs and inline styles.
102-- [Layout-компоненты и отступы](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/layout-ru.md) — В этом руководстве описаны основы layout в UIKit: общая шкала отступов (--g-spacing-*, используемая в токенах и props), адаптивная сетка (Container/Row/Col) и построенные поверх них flexbox-примитивы Flex/Box. Собирайте из них страницы вместо использования сырых div и inline-стилей.
103-- [Server-Side Rendering](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/server-side-rendering.md) — English | Русский
104-- [Theming, Colors & Branding](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/theming.md) — English | Русский
105-- [Typography](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/typography.md) — UIKit's type scale is a fixed set of text variants, each with predefined font-size and line-height. Render text with the Text component and a variant — not raw <h1>/<p> tags or inline font-size. This keeps sizing consistent and theme-aware across the app.
106-- [Интернационализация (I18N)](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/i18n-ru.md) — English | Русский
107-- [Серверный рендеринг (SSR)](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/server-side-rendering-ru.md) — English | Русский
108-- [Темизация, цвета и брендинг](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/guides/theming-ru.md) — English | Русский
--
116-- [Alert](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/Alert.md) — The Alert component displays a prominent message to draw the user's attention to important information.
117-- [ArrowToggle](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/ArrowToggle.md) — ArrowToggle is a component for displaying the chevron icon. It can rotate in four directions and can be used to display drop-down lists, cut components, etc.
118:- [Avatar](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/Avatar.md) — This component is intended for rendering avatars. It has three basic avatar types: image, icon, and text (name initials). All these types have special properties to configure the behavior and appearance.
119-- [AvatarStack](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/AvatarStack.md) — This component is used for a stack of images with overlap over one another and, optionally, a control. It usually refers to user avatars.
120-- [Breadcrumbs](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/Breadcrumbs.md) — Breadcrumbs is a navigation element that shows the current location of a page within a website’s hierarchy. It provides links that allow users to return to higher levels in the hierarchy, making it easier to navigate through a website with multiple layers. Breadcrumbs are especially useful for large websites and applications with hierarchy-based structure of pages.
121-- [Button](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/Button.md) — Buttons act as a trigger for certain actions. While this is their main purpose, in some very rare cases, they can be used as links to navigate to other pages.
122-- [Card](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/Card.md) — Card is a reusable React component that basically is a card-like container with customizable styles and features. It is used to display information or content in a visually appealing and well-organized manner.
123-- [Checkbox](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/Checkbox.md) — The Checkbox component allows the user to select or deselect a specific value.
124-- [ClipboardButton](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/ClipboardButton.md) — ClipboardButton is a ready-made button that copies given text to the clipboard and plays a success animation. It combines CopyToClipboard (the copy behavior) with ClipboardIcon (the animated icon).
125-- [ClipboardIcon](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/ClipboardIcon.md) — ClipboardIcon is an animated copy icon that reflects the copy state (idle or success); it is meant to sit inside CopyToClipboard or ClipboardButton rather than be used on its own.
126-- [controls/PasswordInput](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/controls/PasswordInput.md)
127-- [controls/TextArea](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/controls/TextArea.md)
128-- [controls/TextInput](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/controls/TextInput.md)
129-- [CopyToClipboard](https://unpkg.com/@gravity-ui/uikit@7.51.1/build/docs/components/CopyToClipboard.md) — CopyToClipboard is a render-prop wrapper that copies text to the clipboard and exposes the copy status to its child, letting you render your own trigger; for a ready-made button use ClipboardButton.
